{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/488239-ideas-for-gift-presented-to-the-season-court-leaders","id":488239,"title":"Ideas for gift presented to the season court leaders.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-22T07:22:13-07:00","id":488239,"title":"Ideas for gift presented to the season court leaders.","content":"I writing up a little side story for fun, where my character ( An ogre who was a forge worker in Acadia ) forges gifts for the courts. In our game the direction courts are king, but the seasonal courts have a small presence. I was wondering if anyone might have any ideas as to a gift I could present to the the seasonal courts as a whole or four small gifts that would be appropriate.<br /> For comparison, here is what I thought up for the directional courts:<br /> North: A black shield styled to look like a turtle shell. (The black tortoise is a symbol of theirs.) <br /> East: A Trident in a coiled serpent base.<br /> South: A set of hand crafted paint brushes.<br /> West: A sword<br /> I wrote out several pages of story regarding this but I'm just drawing a blank on trying to come up with something appropriate, I don't want to be as big and flashy with each court for directions because politically they hold little members or clout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5760-comwizz2","name":"comwizz2","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T21:40:05-07:00","id":489015,"title":"","content":"Summer: An iron spear - perhaps even a token spear with a cold iron head, if the ST allows it.<br /> Autumn: Any item with mystical power and significance. This would be best personalized to the monarch in question - maybe a scrying pool or crystal ball, maybe a leaden skull that acts as a receptacle for knowledge, maybe some form of magical wand or scepter.<br /> Winter: A veil of fine silver chain that makes its owner appear unremarkable when worn<br /> Spring: A piece of artwork which inflames desire when gazed upon. Again, probably best personalized to the monarch as to what form it takes. Could also be a piece of clothing which enhances the desirability of the wearer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T07:57:59-07:00","id":489488,"title":"","content":"What HobbitGuy said, though if you're going for the desirability-strengthening accessory for Spring, maybe make it a Crown of Antlers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T18:48:28-07:00","id":490122,"title":"","content":"Heck, make art (or hedgespun tokens) representing all four seasons: a leaden scrying mirror, an antler crown of desire, an iron spear, and an arrow which either never makes a sound or which deadens all sound in the area","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T05:34:35-07:00","id":490423,"title":"","content":"The suggestions so far seem to be more complicated than the Directional Court gifts. It sounds like the OP wants ideas for something simpler than what was given initially. For something shared, perhaps a square mural, with each corner reflecting the colors of a season, or a metal tree, with a quarter reflecting each season (budding, blooming, dying, empty). If you want to give each season a small gift, a mirror or a pair earrings for spring, a simple dagger or a pair of steel-toed shoes for summer, a polished crystal or a bizarre-looking sculpture for autumn, and a single arrow or a hooded cloak for winter might be appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}